##
## Upstream tests to disable
##
## When adding a new filter to this list, please include a short description of
## why the filter is required and create an associated tracking issue.
##

# rust logs severity has been tamed in brave, as crates were spamming CI with
# logs.
-RustLogIntegrationTest.CheckAllSeverity

# Pkey pool tests exhaust the 256MB ThreadIsolatedPool size. The test allocates
# up to 250 random-sized blocks (up to 2MB each) simultaneously, which exceeds
# the pool capacity. This is an upstream test limitation - the test works with
# the regular GiB-sized pool but not the smaller pkey pool.
-AlternateTestParams/PartitionAllocTest.ZeroFill/2
-AlternateTestParams/PartitionAllocTest.ZeroFill/3
-AlternateTestParams/PartitionAllocWithSizedFreeTest.SchedulerLoopQuarantine/2
-AlternateTestParams/PartitionAllocWithSizedFreeTest.SchedulerLoopQuarantine/3

# Upstream Chromium test racing against upstream test infrastructure, not Brave
# code. DelayedTaskManager::ProcessRipeTasks() pops a ripe ThreadPool delayed
# task off delayed_task_queue_ and releases queue_lock_ before the callback
# reaches TaskTracker::RegisterTaskSource(), which is what increments
# num_incomplete_task_sources_. While the task is in flight in that window,
# ThreadPoolImpl::NextScheduledRunTimeForTesting() reports no pending work, so
# TaskEnvironment::FastForwardToNextTaskOrCap() returns kNone and
# FastForwardUntilNoTasksRemain() returns before the delayed task has run
# (reported as "expected 387, actual 131"). The service thread hits that window
# once mock time has already advanced past the task's run time, making its
# wake-up immediate. A fix belongs in base/task/thread_pool/. Upstream LUCI
# Analysis reports the test as stable (0.4% flake rate / 30d), so Brave-specific
# causes were checked first and came up empty: chromium_src/base has nothing
# under base/task or base/test/task_environment*, and no patch touches either.
# Filtered on all platforms rather than in a linux-msan file because the window
# is platform-independent: Brave saw it on linux-x64-asan
# (brave/brave-browser#50832) and linux-x64-msan, and the upstream flakes come
# from non-sanitizer builders across several OSes (linux-chromeos-rel,
# android-x64-rel, linux-rel, mac-rel, win-rel, ios-simulator).
# https://github.com/brave/brave-browser/issues/57983
-TaskEnvironmentTest.MultiThreadedMockTimeAndThreadPoolQueuedMode
